  "witness": "a repairable pre-N error with its declared bounded repair recipe continues, is repaired by N and stays in the report as corrected",
  "derivation": "Profile = export.prepare.success profile + an Association notion/glyph + the repairable rule and its normalize repair recipe (set associationDirection None on associations without one). DESIGN \u00a76.2: 'a repairable pre-N error may continue only with its declared bounded repair recipe; post-N unresolved errors block'; \u00a76.4: 'corrected pre-N findings remain history with disposition corrected'. The rule assoc-direction (phase pre-normalize, classification repairable, repairRecipe assoc-direction-fix, accept severity error) finds Assoc_1 without associationDirection. The pre-normalize stage does not block on it; N applies assoc-direction-fix (one normalize/set change entry with the written-location coordinates /rootElements/0/artifacts/1/associationDirection, lot-3 vocabulary and harmonization B8/B9); the post-normalize lint finds nothing, so the pre-N finding is reported with disposition corrected. Layout, R and map run on the staged tree (Assoc_1 now carries associationDirection None): page e_0, nodes s-note e_1 'helper', s-task-a e_2, s-task-b e_3; four capability semantic-type losses (the association edge included). The complete report lists the corrected finding, the N change entry and the losses in stage order; the Result keeps the input revision (read-only) while the prepared artifact and its renderBinding carry the staged revision. Options are validated before the pipeline (closed option record, format declared with a registered adapter, theme resolvable; harmonization C18); then each stage runs exactly once on a staged deep copy in the DESIGN \u00a710.2 order compatibility -> graph checks -> C -> pre-normalize -> N -> post-normalize -> layout -> post-layout -> release -> R -> map under the accept policy, edit activation; the sealed trace lists the stages the observer saw, in order. A refusal returns the complete report of the executed lint stages (no change entry, no candidate) and no artifact (harmonization B2); no input is mutated.",
